<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Companion gene for the psychic transceiver hediff. NOT player-assignable.
    Managed entirely by Hediff_PsychicTransceiver (added on install, removed on uninstall).

    Purpose: Overrides the android's inherent psychic insensitivity. VREA encodes
    this machine-nature trait as the VREA_PsychicallyDeaf gene (PsychicSensitivity
    factor of zero). The shared AAH_AndroidPsychic exclusion tag causes Biotech to
    suppress VREA_PsychicallyDeaf while this gene is active, removing the zero factor.
    Since that was a x0 factor (not a base change), PsychicSensitivity returns to its
    100% StatDef base, on which the hediff's own PsychicSensitivity offset then stacks.
    The VREA_GenePatches.xml XPath patch adds this exclusion tag to VREA_PsychicallyDeaf.

    canGenerateInGeneSet: false prevents this from appearing in xenotype creation.
    biostatArc > 0 is required for the archite gene background (see modExtensions).

    Background rendering: Uses VEF's GeneExtension.backgroundPathArchite instead of
    the standard endogenes/xenogenes background path. VEF's transpiler in
    GeneUIUtility.DrawGene selects this archite background when biostatArc > 0.

    Icon: References the vanilla Biotech psy-sensitive gene icon directly from the
    game's asset bundle. No custom texture needed.

    Display: VREA's custom gene inspector only shows genes its Utils.IsAndroidGene
    check recognises. The Utils_IsAndroidGene patch extends that check to all
    AAH_Hardware-category genes, which also relabels biostatMet as "Power
    efficiency" and rolls it into the inspector's Power efficiency total.

    Locked: declared as VREAndroids.AndroidGeneDef with isCoreComponent=true so VREA's
    behavior-station modify dialog treats it like core hardware — Utils.CanBeRemovedFromAndroid
    returns false, so it can't be removed by clicking in the dialog (as with VREA's own
    reactor/body genes). Removal stays exclusive to our surgery recipes / hediff hooks.
  -->
  <VREAndroids.AndroidGeneDef>
    <defName>AAH_PsychicTransceiver</defName>
    <label>psychic transceiver</label>
    <description>Androids with this hardware are sensitive to psychic energy and influence, despite their synthetic nature. Once awakened, the opened mind remains susceptible to outside direction — at a behavior station it will again accept reprogramming it would otherwise refuse.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Hardware/Gene_PsychicTransceiver</iconPath>
    <!-- <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_EnhancedPsychicAbility</iconPath> -->
    <displayCategory>AAH_Hardware</displayCategory>
    <displayOrderInCategory>5</displayOrderInCategory>
    <canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
    <isCoreComponent>true</isCoreComponent>
    <biostatArc>1</biostatArc>
    <biostatCpx>4</biostatCpx>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>AAH_AndroidPsychic</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Genes.GeneExtension">
        <backgroundPathArchite>UI/Icons/Genes/GeneBackground_ArchotechHardware</backgroundPathArchite>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VREAndroids.AndroidGeneDef>

</Defs>